kicad_pcb_version: placeholder

# NOTE: This is a placeholder .kicad_pcb file for the KiCad project.
# It contains placement and PCB rules/comments only. To convert this into
# a working KiCad PCB, open KiCad and create a new PCB using the provided
# placement_and_pcb_rules.md and schematic netlist. This file is a draft
# to be replaced by a generated .kicad_pcb from KiCad PCBNew export.

# Placement notes (repeat of placement_and_pcb_rules.md):
# - Place RCA connectors on the left edge (J_RCA_IN1..3, J_RCA_OUT)
# - Place TDA7439 close to RCA_INs
# - Place MCP6002 near TDA outputs and RCA_OUT
# - Place MCU and UI (OLED, encoder) on right/front panel side
# - Provide testpoints for V_3V3, V_AUDIO, I2C_SCL, I2C_SDA, TDA_OUT_L/R

# Layer stack (recommended):
# L1 Top: components and most signals
# L2 GND: full ground plane
# L3 PWR: power plane (V_AUDIO/V_3V3)
# L4 Bottom: signals

# DRC suggestions:
# - Min track width: 0.2 mm for signals, larger for power
# - Net classes: AUDIO (0.3 mm), I2C (0.2 mm), POWER (1.0 mm)

# NOTE: Replace this placeholder with the PCB generated by KiCad (File->Export-> PCB) or use the kicad CLI tools to generate a valid .kicad_pcb.
